# Saving into the mere session, the editor's Undo save, and Graphshell's
# session Undo (Scenograph editor plan, E2b; SE14 to SE22). A save is stored
# by the frame pump without holding the host across the write; `settle 6`
# gives the write its frames before the store state is read.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
act open-projection-editor
settle 2
dom click [data-projection-panel="preview"]
settle 2
type #gs-projection-appearance-title Stored one
settle 2
act save-projection
settle 6
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-status Saved
assert snap session-store == stored
type #gs-projection-appearance-title Stored two
settle 2
act save-projection
settle 6
assert snap session-store == stored
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-dirty No unsaved changes
act undo-projection-save
settle 6
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-status Undid save · Graphshell reference projection
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-preview Stored one ·
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-dirty No unsaved changes
assert snap session-store == stored
# The stored definition came back as one step on the draft's own history.
act undo-projection
settle 2
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-preview Stored two ·
act redo-projection
settle 2
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-preview Stored one ·
act redo-projection-save
settle 6
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-status Redid save
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-preview Stored two ·
# Graphshell's session Undo reaches its own change, never the editor's save.
type #gs-address-input https://example.net/session-undo-probe
settle 2
act node:new
settle 2
act session:undo
settle 6
assert dom #gs-product-status Undid Graphshell's last change
assert dom #gs-projection-editor-preview Stored two ·
assert snap session-store == stored
capture projection_session
wait
log projection session save and undo proof complete
